    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0843" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4468: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul in Charge at Canton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Huston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-16T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 16—9:47
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Chen’s<anchor n="55" xml:id="d487-f1"/> troops seized Canton 3 o’clock morning,
                    declare constitutional government at end and in favor of old Parliament. Sun’s
                    body guards still fighting in President’s palace. Sun supposed escaped Whampoa
                    on gunboat.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d487-f1" n="55" xml:id="d487-f1-content">
                <p>Chen Chiung-ming; Governor of Kwangtung, Commander in Chief of Kwangtung troops;
                    and concurrent Minister of War in the Canton Government.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
